          "modify_from": "Use the complete motion: a momentary 'held' label does not establish lifting, and incidental peg movement does not establish tool use.",
          "modify_to": "Prioritize the coherent motion after gripper closure and during cube displacement over object detections. The initial open-hand descent from a raised position is not a pickup lift, nor is a small variation in tabletop height. Classify as \"hook\" only when the demonstration shows a coherent peg grasp, subsequent raising, and use of that grasped tool to move the cube. Changing peg detections, visible head/tail labels, or incidental peg displacement alone do not establish hooking. Classify as \"lift\" when a cube grasp is followed by raising and carrying the cube. When the fingers close essentially fully and the hand moves the cube at sustained tabletop height without lifting either cube or peg, classify as \"push\", even if peg detections change or the cube is temporarily occluded. A momentary 'held' label does not establish lifting."
        },
        {
          "modify_from": "If demonstration evidence is inconclusive, write \"unknown\" and retain it.",
          "modify_to": "If demonstration evidence is inconclusive, write \"unknown\" and retain it. Do not use \"unknown\" merely because object detections fluctuate when the motion evidence establishes the method."
        }
      ]
    }
